    lead:"The Reconstruction Truce, also called the November Understanding, was the informal arrangement that allowed Aneurin Bevan's minority government and the fragmented Brick Parliament to conduct urgent postwar business. It was not a coalition, confidence-and-supply treaty, or written constitutional compact.",
